Q.  Explain Shadow DOM and Light DOM?
Shadow DOM provides component encapsulation.
Every LWC component gets its own private DOM, which prevents CSS and JavaScript from affecting other components.
Eg. Component A doesn’t effect component B
Advantages
✅ Encapsulation
✅ Better Security
✅ Prevents CSS Conflicts
✅ Reusable Components

Light DOM
Light DOM allows a component's content to participate in the regular document DOM structure.
Advantages of Light DOM
✅ Easier integration with third-party libraries
✅ Better accessibility in some cases
✅ Easier DOM querying
✅ Better for analytics tools




Shadow DOM vs Light DOM
Feature	Shadow DOM	Light DOM
Encapsulation	Yes	No
CSS Isolation	Yes	No
Security	High	Lower
Third-party Library Access	Limited	Easy
Default in LWC	Yes	No

