Q: If an Apex class is with sharing and called from LWC, but the user doesn't have access to the queried records, will it throw an error?
Answer:
No, with sharing respects Salesforce record-sharing rules. The query returns only records the user can access. If the user has no access, the query returns zero records (empty list). An exception occurs only when the code expects a single record and no record is returned, such as assigning a SOQL result directly to an SObject variable. with sharing controls record-level access, not CRUD/FLS security.











 
 




































































































	



